---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="About">
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>About Servare Opus</h1>
      <p>Executive support built on a simple idea: most CEOs share the same problems.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section>
    <div class="container prose">
      <p>Servare Opus was built around a simple observation: most CEOs and founders don't need a full-time executive assistant sitting idle between tasks — they need someone senior, sharp, and fully engaged for the hours that matter. So we built a firm around a fractional model, matching experienced EAs with a small, deliberately chosen roster of CEOs at a time.</p>

      <h2>How the model works</h2>
      <p>Each Servare Opus executive assistant supports a handful of CEOs — never so many that you're competing for attention, never so few that you're paying full-time rates for part-time needs. Your EA gets to know your business, your calendar rhythms, and your preferences well enough to work independently, while still costing a fraction of a dedicated hire.</p>

      <h2>Who we work with</h2>
      <p>Founders, CEOs, and senior executives at growing companies who need real operational relief — not another tool to manage. Clients typically come to us buried in scheduling conflicts, travel logistics, or board prep, and leave with hours of their week back.</p>

      <h2>Discretion, first</h2>
      <p>Executive support only works if it's trustworthy. Every Servare Opus EA is vetted for judgment and discretion before they're matched with a client, and every engagement is treated as confidential by default.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt">
    <div class="container" style="text-align:center;">
      <h2>Ready to get some of your week back?</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--gray); max-width:520px; margin: 0 auto 28px;">Start with a no-pressure discovery call. We'll talk through where your time is going and whether we're a fit.</p>
      <a href="/booking" class="btn">Book a Discovery Call</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
